# **A native image decoder fed attacker-supplied bytes** -- the same category
# as `av` above, and the same rule applies: bumping this pin is a security
# action, not a chore. `uploads.validation` calls `Image.open()` on every
# upload and `uploads.tasks` / `uploads.image_utils` decode and re-encode
# them, so every CVE in a decoder Pillow will try is directly reachable.
#
# Pillow 13.0.0 fixes the October 2026 decoder/encoder advisories, including
# TIFF buffer reads, PDF parser stack exhaustion, and GIF decompression checks.
# https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/releasenotes/13.0.0.html
# Python 3.12 remains supported; the production image uses its binary wheel.
Pillow==13.0.0
